{
  "_comment": "INDUSTRIAL: an open battery rack - a dark tray, two end cheeks, four cells standing in a row and one yellow bus bar bolted across their terminals. The rack is OPEN because exposure is the kit's thesis: a sold ship would fair this over, a working ship wants the cells where a fitter can swap one. The bus bar is the kit's yellow in its COLLAR use, same paint as the stack's collar - the accent stays a system (edges, collars, handles) rather than a colour. Long axis is +Z so `align: Run` lies the rack down the deck grain with the ducts and the radiator fins.",
